        "text": "Now that you have some basic understanding of blockchain technology, it's time to take a look at its first implementation as cryptocurrencies. A cryptocurrency is a type of digital currency that is maintained by a decentralized blockchain. Currencies are a part of the monetary system, and money is a system of transferring value between parties, especially for the purpose of trade. But what exactly is value? Value is a shared belief. If you think about it, there's no such thing as inherent value. Sure, something like a natural resource arguably has value that's usually tied to its utility, how useful it is. But regardless, the concept of value is an entirely human creation. People want things for all sorts of reasons.",
